{
  "slug": "php-harmony",
  "name": "Php Harmony",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Comprehensive PHP development toolkit with code quality enforcement, ORM patterns, async messaging guidance, security auditing, and automated quality hooks. Supports\nSymfony 6/7 and any Composer-based PHP project. Includes auto-invoked skills for coding conventions, Doctrine, Messenger, testing, and security — plus commands,\nspecialized agents, and post-save hooks for debug detection and auto-formatting.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **5 skills**, **3 agents**, **5 commands** and **1 hook**.\n\n- **Skills** (5): `doctrine-patterns` (Doctrine ORM patterns and best practices for Symfony), `messenger-patterns` (Symfony Messenger component patterns for async processing), `symfony-conventions` (PHP and Symfony coding conventions and best practices), `symfony-security` (Symfony security patterns for authentication and authorization), `testing-patterns` (PHP and Symfony testing patterns with PHPUnit)\n- **Agents** (3): `php-code-reviewer` (Reviews PHP and Symfony code for bugs, anti-patterns, convention violations, and quality issues), `security-auditor` (Audits PHP and Symfony code for security vulnerabilities including injection, XSS, CSRF, authentication flaws, and dependency vulnerabilities), `symfony-architect` (Analyzes Symfony project architecture, maps module boundaries, evaluates service dependencies, and provides architectural recommendations)\n- **Commands** (5): `check-debug` (Scan the codebase for leftover debug statements (dd, dump, var_dump, die, ray, etc.)), `doctrine-migration` (Generate, review, and manage Doctrine database migrations), `quality-check` (Run PHP code quality tools (PHPStan, PHP-CS-Fixer) on the project or a specific path), `run-tests` (Run PHPUnit tests with optional filter, coverage reporting, and parallel execution), `symfony-make` (Generate Symfony components (entity, controller, command, message, voter, form, subscriber) following project conventions)\n- **Hooks** (1): `PostToolUse`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install php-harmony@claude-community` from `MaartenDeRammelaere1/php-symfony-toolkit`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 5,
    "agent": 3,
    "hook": 1,
    "command": 5
  },
